    "opening": "A limited liability company, or LLC, is a business entity created under state law. Its legal structure is separate from its federal tax classification. Compare ownership, management, funding obligations and recordkeeping before choosing it; the label alone does not establish tax savings, eliminate every personal risk or make a business profitable.",
    "answerHtml": "<p>A limited liability company, or LLC, is a business entity created under state law. Its legal structure is separate from its federal tax classification. Compare ownership, management, funding obligations and recordkeeping before choosing it; the label alone does not establish tax savings, eliminate every personal risk or make a business profitable.</p>",
