    "title": "Cloud Accounting: Workflow, Controls and Migration Review",
    "seoTitle": "Cloud Accounting: Workflow and Controls",
    "description": "Evaluate cloud accounting through workflows, access controls, reconciliation and exit records. Check an original migration case before comparing complete costs.",
    "metaDescription": "Evaluate cloud accounting through workflows, access controls, reconciliation and exit records. Check an original migration case before comparing complete costs.",
    "primaryKeyword": "cloud accounting",
    "scopeBoundary": "Owns choosing and operating a cloud-accounting workflow and its record controls; not a ranked software roundup, vendor-price list or a replacement for bookkeeping rules.",
    "opening": "Cloud accounting uses remotely hosted software to record transactions, reconcile accounts and prepare reports. Assess it through a complete workflow: capture evidence, approve entries, reconcile balances, close the period and export usable records. A bank connection or dashboard is helpful only when people, classifications and controls produce a trustworthy ledger.",
    "answerHtml": "<p>Cloud accounting uses remotely hosted software to record transactions, reconcile accounts and prepare reports. Assess it through a complete workflow: capture evidence, approve entries, reconcile balances, close the period and export usable records. A bank connection or dashboard is helpful only when people, classifications and controls produce a trustworthy ledger.</p>",
    "answerTitle": "Quick answer",
